cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How Faithful Is the Circuit You Found? Post-Selection-Valid
  Confidence Bounds for Mechanistic Interpretability
message: If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ihor
    family-names: Kendiukhov
    email: ihor.kendiukhov@student.uni-tuebingen.de
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Medical Genetics and Applied Genomics, University of
      Tuebingen, Tuebingen, Germany
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Kendiukhov/post-selection-faithfulness'
abstract: >-
  A library and a set of experiments for lower confidence bounds on the graded
  faithfulness of a mechanistic circuit hypothesis that remain valid however the
  circuit was selected: empirical-Bernstein union bounds, prior-weighted (Occam)
  bounds over power sets of components, empirical bootstrap-t simultaneous bands,
  cluster-robust variants, sample splitting, and selective (polyhedral) intervals.
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - causal abstraction
  - post-selection inference
  - selective inference
  - bootstrap
  - confidence bounds
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
